# ── Movement chain (frontend reads NEXT_PUBLIC_* at build time) ─────────────
# Copy to .env.local for local dev; set the same keys on Vercel (Production).
# Never commit .env.local or .movement/ (see .gitignore).
#
# Official URLs (rate limits may apply — see docs):
#   CLI:     https://docs.movementnetwork.xyz/devs/movementcli
#   RPCs:    https://docs.movementnetwork.xyz/devs/networkEndpoints
#   Status:  https://status.movementnetwork.xyz/

# Fullnode REST — path must include /v1 (primary endpoints from Network Endpoints doc).

# Testnet — Chain ID 250
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MOVEMENT_RPC_URL=https://testnet.movementnetwork.xyz/v1

# Mainnet — Chain ID 126 (use after publish; replace MODULE_ADDRESS)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MOVEMENT_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.movementnetwork.xyz/v1

# ── Solana (Phase 4) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The browser only reads NEXT_PUBLIC_* values. Keep ORACLE_KEYPAIR server-only.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_CLUSTER=devnet
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOVEMATCH_PROGRAM_ID=A8UiSCd5yzhpZZwmop6k5upLVxUhDZq3x9pq7SfwoKN5
NEXT_PUBLIC_USDC_MINT=4zMMC9srt5Ri5X14GAgXhaHii3GnPAEERYPJgZJDncDU
#
# JSON array of the oracle signer secret key. Never prefix this variable with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never expose it to the browser.
# ORACLE_KEYPAIR=[...]
#
# Both oracle files below default to being served by this app out of public/data,
# so neither variable is required. The admin page downloads each file after the
# on-chain commit; move it into the repo and deploy:
#   stats-<gw>.json   -> public/data/stats/<gw>.json
#   results-<gw>.json -> public/data/results/<gw>.json
# Set the variables only to move publishing to external object storage.
#
# Object-storage location holding the results + Merkle proofs published by the
# oracle. Server-only: /api/results proxies it so the bucket stays unexposed.
# RESULTS_PUBLISH_BUCKET=https://results.example.com/movematch
#
# Public base URL of the committed stats files (<base>/<gameweek>.json). This one
# is public on purpose: StatsCommit stores the hash, so anyone can re-verify it.
# The URI goes on-chain and cannot be edited, so mainnet refuses to commit stats
# unless this is set explicitly.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STATS_BASE_URL=https://results.example.com/movematch/stats

# Legacy alias (optional; used only if NEXT_PUBLIC_MOVEMENT_RPC_URL is empty)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APTOS_API=https://testnet.movementnetwork.xyz/v1

# Account where the fantasy_epl package is published (32-byte hex)
NEXT_PUBLIC_MODULE_ADDRESS=0xf598f059a0353b0d9ea80c9fd9d1c3e15b71ff4535388dd79acf813b567c5b47

# Module name inside that package
NEXT_PUBLIC_MODULE_NAME=fantasy_epl

# World Cup campaign as primary product surface (homepage hero, nav, ticker).
# Default / unset = true. Set false after the tournament to restore EPL focus.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WC_CAMPAIGN_ACTIVE=false

# ── Stableyard cross-chain deposit (optional) ───────────────────────────────
# Shows “Deposit from another chain” on squad pages when wallet is connected.
# Set to false to hide the widget without removing the integration code.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STABLEYARD_ENABLED=true

# ── USDCx entry fee (production default) ───────────────────────────────────
# Squad registration + prizes use USDCx (5 USDC = 5_000_000 on-chain).
# Frontend reads get_entry_fee_asset from chain; defaults to USDCx if view missing.
# Activation checklist: move/USDCX_ENTRY_FEE_PREP.md

# ── Referral tracking ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Referral links: share https://<site>/?ref=<code>. Clicks + registrations are
# attributed per code. Dashboard: /admin/referrals
#
# REFERRAL_ADMIN_KEY — required to view /api/referral/stats and the dashboard.
#   If unset, the stats endpoint is disabled (503). Pick any long random string.
# REFERRAL_ADMIN_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
#
# Durable storage (optional but recommended for production). Create a free
# Upstash Redis DB (https://upstash.com) → copy the REST URL + token.
# Without these, tracking uses a process-local in-memory store that resets on
# every serverless cold start (fine for local dev, lossy in production).
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://<your-db>.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=<your-rest-token>

# ── World Cup 2026 match data (football-data.org, FREE) ────────────────────
# Free source for WC schedule / scores / deadlines (display only — decoupled from
# the API-Sports player oracle). Register for a token (free tier covers WC 2026):
#   https://www.football-data.org/client/register
# Powers /api/wc-fixtures and /api/wc-live; without it those fall back to the
# static public/data/wc-fixtures.json. Also used by /admin → Pull from API for
# the homepage hero bracket state.
# FOOTBALL_DATA_TOKEN=your-football-data-org-token
#
# WC_BRACKET_STATE_ADMIN_KEY — required to publish official group/knockout state
# to the homepage hero via /admin (PUT /api/wc-bracket-state). Pick a long random string.
# WC_BRACKET_STATE_ADMIN_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# ── World Cup 2026 player stats (API-Sports, PAID) ─────────────────────────
# Per-player oracle stats + squads require a paid API-Sports plan (free tier is
# locked to seasons 2022-2024). Used by scripts/fetch-wc-players.mjs and the
# oracle submit flow. Squads and stats MUST share this single source (apiId).
# API_SPORTS_KEY=your-api-sports-key

# ── Before mainnet ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1) npm run move:test && npm run build
# 2) npm run preflight:mainnet  (with mainnet RPC + new address in .env.local)
# 3) movement move publish … from move/fantasy-epl-contract (see Movement CLI doc)
# 4) Vercel: update env → Redeploy. See move/MAINNET_CHECKLIST.txt
